    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. First, apply the exponent rule.\n2. Then, distribute.\n3. Lastly, perform the addition in the expression. To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will use the binomial theorem. Let's go through the steps in detail:\n\n1. **First, apply the exponent rule:**\n   The binomial theorem states that \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\). Here, \\(a = 2x\\) and \\(b = 5\\). So, we have:\n   \\[\n   (2x + 5)^2 = (2x)^2 + 2 \\cdot 2x \\cdot 5 + 5^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Then, distribute:**\n   First, compute \\( (2x)^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   (2x)^2 = 4x^2\n   \\]\n   Next, compute \\(2 \\cdot 2x \\cdot 5\\):\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 2x \\cdot 5 = 20x\n   \\]\n   Finally, compute \\(5^2\\):\n   \\[\n   5^2 = 25\n   \\]\n\n3. **Lastly, perform the addition in the expression:**\n   \\[\n   4x^2 + 20x + 25\n   \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression:\n\\[\n4(3)^2 + 20(3) + 25\n\\]\n\n4. **Calculate the square and the products:**\n   \\[\n   4(3)^2 = 4 \\cdot 9 = 36\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   20(3) = 60\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   36 + 60 + 25 = 121\n   \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).\n\nThe decision-making process involved in assigning responsibility for functional departments is the ____ stage in the performance management system. A. Implementation stage B. Planning stage C. Appraisal phase D. Interview stage\nA. The decision-making process involved in assigning responsibility for functional departments is the () stage in the performance management system.\nA. Implementation stage\nB. Planning stage\nC. Appraisal phase\nD. Interview stage\nAnswer:\nC\n\nA higher percentage of total energy expended by offspring compared to parents' treadmill test can be associated with which of the following recorded results?\nA. More frequent exercise\nB. More rapid gain in total food intake\nC. Development of improved cardiovascular functions with health benefits\nD. Enhanced sense of body shape satisfaction and self-confidence\nAnswer:\nC\n\nPatient, male, 56 years old. For 10 years, he has suffered from hypertensive heart disease. Recently, after overwork, he suddenly developed syncope and deep, fast breathing once. His symptoms have been responsive to sublingual nitroglycerin administration. One hour later, he developed shortness of breath, unable to lie flat, and had cyanosis of the lips. What is the primary treatment for this condition?\nA. Administer succinylates intravenous drip\nB. Administer metoprolol intravenous drip\nC. Intravenous injection of dexamethasone\nD. Add pethidine as a premedication\nE. Intravenous injection of furosemide\nAnswer:\n\nA\n\nWhich of the following is NOT a role that children's research and experimental education may have?\nA. Pursuing knowledge as a passion\nB. Enhancing understanding of the world\nC. A means to pursue fame and fortune\nD. Developing critical thinking and innovative ability\nAnswer:\nC\n\nA patient had a programming competition at school but felt threatened by others and was later informed that they had not paid their school tuition. Which of the following rights did the primary school infringe upon?\nA. Right toeducation\nB. Righttohealth\nC. Righttoliteracy\nD. Righttodesignerecessarymedicalmedicines\nAnswer:\nA",
